------------------------------
=F0=9F=8D=9D Espagueti Rojo (from the video) =F0=9F=A7=BE Ingredients

*(based on what=E2=80=99s shown in the video steps + typical ingredients us=
ed
there)*

   - Spaghetti
   - Tomatoes (jitomate)
   - Onion
   - Garlic
   - Butter
   - Cream (for creamy texture)
   - Salt or chicken bouillon
   - Water
   - Optional: cheese for serving

These ingredients match what=E2=80=99s used in the video=E2=80=99s process =
(tomato sauce
blended with onion/garlic, cooked in butter, then finished with cream and
cheese). [youtube.com] <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DlHmT7ipGNY4>
------------------------------
=F0=9F=91=A9=E2=80=8D=F0=9F=8D=B3 Steps (simple + clear) 1. Make the tomato=
 sauce

   - Blend tomatoes, onion, garlic, and a little water until smooth
   - Strain if desired for a smoother sauce [youtube.com]
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DlHmT7ipGNY4>

2. Cook the sauce

   - Melt butter in a pot
   - Pour in the tomato mixture
   - Cook about *20 minutes* on medium heat
   - Season with salt or chicken bouillon [youtube.com]
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DlHmT7ipGNY4>

3. Add cream

   - Turn off the heat
   - Slowly mix in the cream (stir well so it doesn=E2=80=99t curdle) [yout=
ube.com]
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DlHmT7ipGNY4>

4. Cook the spaghetti

   - Boil water with:
      - onion
      - garlic
      - salt
      - a little oil
   - Add spaghetti and cook until *al dente (~10 minutes)* [youtube.com]
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DlHmT7ipGNY4>

5. Combine everything

   - Drain the pasta
   - Add it to the sauce
   - Mix well and heat together for a few minutes [youtube.com]
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DlHmT7ipGNY4>

6. Serve

   - Plate the spaghetti
   - Top with cheese if you like

------------------------------
=F0=9F=92=A1 Helpful tips (based on the video)

   - Cooking the sauce longer deepens the flavor
   - Add cream slowly to avoid separation
   - Mixing the pasta with the sauce at the end helps it absorb flavor


